 prop. It provides consistent spacing, elevation, rounding, and self-alignment within flex or grid containers."],[874,"`BoxContext` supplies default props to Boxes in its subtree. A `slots` map supplies defaults to\nnamed parts; each Box selects one with `slot`. Explicit consumer props override defaults, while\nclasses, styles, and refs are merged. Pass `slot={null}` to opt out of the context."],[520,"`Button slot=\"trigger\"` renders a native button with `aria-expanded` for its open state and\n`aria-controls` linked to the panel automatically."],[170,"`Calendar` values are `CalendarDate` objects. Import the date primitives you need from the `@godaddy/antares/date` subpath:"],[201,"`CardGroup` uses grid navigation: Tab enters or leaves, arrow keys move between Cards, and Space\nchanges selection. Enter activates row actions or links. Choose selection or `onAction`;\ncombining them prevents pointer selection."],[381,"`CheckboxGroup` is composed: write `Label`, a `Group` holding the `Checkbox` items, `Text slot=\"description\"`, and `FieldError`. The `Group` takes its axis, gap, and presentational role from the group's `orientation`, so a bare `<Group>` is all you need; pass your own `direction`/`gap` to lay the items out differently. Each `Checkbox` takes label text next to the indicator."],[442,"`ChipButton` for menu filters and other actions with a Chip-like appearance"],[454,"`ChipButton` is a real button and exposes menu state through `MenuTrigger`; provide an accessible name when the visible content is incomplete."],[438,"`ChipGroup` + `ChipList` + `Chip` for grouped values, selection, keyboard navigation, and removal"],[447,"`ChipGroup` owns selection and removal behavior. Use a Chip render prop for\nstate-dependent content, and `Button` with `slot=\"remove\"` together with\n`onRemove` for removable items. See **Toggle Chips** and **Removable Chips**."],[1701,"`className` and `style` apply to the tooltip panel."],[148,"`CloseButton` dismisses an overlay: it defaults to `slot=\"close\"` and renders an `x` icon labelled \"Close\"."],[515,"`Collapsible`: `data-expanded`, `data-disabled`, and `data-focus-visible-within`."],[521,"`CollapsiblePanel` is labeled by its trigger through `aria-labelledby` automatically."],[522,"`CollapsiblePanel` uses `role=\"group\"` by default. Keep it when the panel's content does not need\na navigation landmark; there is no need to set it explicitly."],[517,"`CollapsiblePanel`: `data-focus-visible-within`."],[564,"`commitBehavior` on `DateRangePickerCalendar` applies to both presentations."],[1157,"`currentStep` is the single source of truth for the timeline. Omit it for a not-yet-started flow where every step is `future`; pass the step count for a fully completed flow where every step is `past`."],[732,"`data-color`: Applied when color prop is set"],[735,"`data-flip`: Applied when flip prop is set (\"horizontal\" or \"vertical\")"],[731,"`data-icon`: The icon name (always present)"],[733,"`data-loading`: Applied during icon loading from CDN"],[734,"`data-mode`: Applied when mode prop is set (e.g., \"sprite\")"],[736,"`data-rotate`: Applied when rotate prop is set (90, 180, or 270)"],[1456,"`data-selected`, `data-hovered`, `data-pressed`, `data-focused`, `data-focus-visible`, `data-disabled`, `data-readonly`, `data-invalid`, `data-required`, `data-size`"],[1386,"`default`, `full`, and `none` rounding"],[562,"`drawerProps` customizes the drawer, which defaults to `85dvh`; `popoverProps` customizes the popover."],[582,"`DrawerTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Drawer>`, handling open\nstate automatically."],[653,"`emphasis` picks a feedback color and changes only the color."],[1620,"`emphasis` picks a feedback color and changes only the color."],[640,"`FileTrigger` adds no visuals or ARIA of its own — accessibility comes from the pressable child you provide. Use a component with an accessible name (e.g. an Antares `Button` with clear label text) so assistive technology announces the action. The underlying `<input>` is visually hidden but remains operable by keyboard through the child's press behavior."],[886,"`Flex` is a one-dimensional layout component for arranging children in rows or columns with alignment and spacing control. It extends `Box`, inheriting all `Box` capabilities (padding, elevation, rounding, self-alignment, and polymorphic `as` prop)."],[740,"`focusable=\"false\"`: Prevents keyboard focus"],[908,"`Grid` is a two-dimensional CSS Grid layout component for complex grid-based layouts. It extends `Box`, inheriting all `Box` capabilities (padding, elevation, rounding, self-alignment, and polymorphic `as` prop)."],[525,"`Icon slot=\"indicator\"` is decorative and receives `aria-hidden=\"true\"` automatically."],[818,"`InlineDrawerPanel` is the collapsible content for the accordion pattern — a thin wrapper over RAC `DisclosurePanel` t"],[810,"`InlineDrawerPanel` is the collapsible content for the accordion pattern — a thin wrapper over RAC `DisclosurePanel` that hides when collapsed. The trigger is any component you slot in with `slot=\"trigger\"` — there's no dedicated trigger component."],[833,"`Input` is the single-line control inside a field, not a field on its own. Prefer `TextField` or `NumberField` as the parent; see those components for fuller examples."],[863,"`lg` - Large spacing"],[934,"`ListBox` requires either `aria-label` or `aria-labelledby`. For a labeled, popover-style picker, prefer `Select`."],[862,"`md` - Medium spacing"],[953,"`MenuTrigger` wraps a trigger element and a `Popover` containing `Menu`. The menu is fully keyboard-navigable, supports typeahead search, and handles open/close state automatically. The trigger applies `hideArrow` and card styling to all popovers, including nested submenus."],[168,"`minValue` / `maxValue` bounds and `isDateUnavailable` per-day disabling"],[1016,"`ModalTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Modal>`, handling open state automatically. Based on RAC `DialogTrigger`."],[1156,"`orientation` switches between `horizontal` (accent bar on top) and `vertical` (accent bar on the leading edge)."],[1502,"`overflowLabels` is optional and defaults to \"Previous tabs\" and \"Next tabs\". Provide localized labels when needed; they should describe the logical direction rather than physical directions like \"left\" or \"right\", as the component automatically handles RTL layouts."],[1696,"`overlay` elevation panel positioned relative to its trigger, with an optional arrow"],[561,"`overlay=\"popover\"` always uses the desktop presentation."],[563,"`pageCount` sets months per popover page: one for single dates and two for ranges by default."],[1064,"`PaginationDots` is decorative and does not replace interactive page\ncontrols."],[825,"`placement` does not flip in RTL; the side is decided by document/flex order."],[813,"`placement` selects the collapse axis (`left`/`right` → width, `top`/`bottom` → height)"],[1081,"`PopoverTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Popover>`, handling open state and positioning automatically.\nBased on RAC `DialogTrigger`. To anchor a popover to an element it doesn't wrap, pass `triggerRef` instead.\nA parent can set `hideArrow` and `containerProps` through `PopoverContext`. Props on `Popover` still win."],[816,"`prefers-reduced-motion` support"],[1109,"`Pressable` accepts the React Aria press props, including `onPress`, `onPressStart`, `onPressEnd`, `onPressUp`, and `onPressChange`."],[1114,"`Pressable` automatically applies React Aria state attributes such as `[data-hovered]`, `[data-pressed]`, `[data-focus-visible]`, and `[data-disabled]` to the child. Ensure the child component styles these states appropriately if it overrides the default `Pressable` styles."],[1197,"`RadioGroup` is composed: write `Label`, a `Group` holding the `Radio` items, `Text slot=\"description\"`, and `FieldError`. The `Group` takes its axis, gap, and presentational role from the group's `orientation`, so a bare `<Group>` is all you need; pass your own `